{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"fervent-cultish-sanderling","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n5 of the 9 local `make verify` logs of Nov 19-20 2026 ran inside the Claude Code agent sandbox (their pytest temp dirs sit under `/private/tmp/claude-502`, the sandbox TMPDIR, and pip reports the sandbox proxy's `Tunnel connection failed: 403 not in this command's allowed_domains`). Those 5 runs each failed 37 to 45 tests that pass in CI. The 4 complete unsandboxed runs of the same days (temp dirs under `/var/folders`) failed only the then-red `test_resign_makes_enforced_verify_pass_with_era_keys` (fixed by 2825b4fe283) and, once, the review-bot 3 s marker tracked in stinky-blushing-gelding.\n\n## Verified cause\nA controlled A/B on Nov 20 2026 ran one fixed set of 21 test modules (logs `.rebar/scratch/s05f74084-f2/ab-sandboxed.log` and `ab-unsandboxed.log` in worktree f2-verify-parity) (origin/main 8e1d15e664f, `-n 4`, same host, minutes apart, load average 17-21) inside and then outside the sandbox. Outside the sandbox all 379 tests passed in 187.58 s. Inside, 18 tests failed and 3 errored (655.42 s); the failures come from 3 capabilities the sandbox denies and the suite needs:\n- AF_UNIX sockets. `socket(AF_UNIX).bind()` under the temp dir raises `PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted`. Breaks all 9 tests in `tests/unit/test_reclaim_resign.py` (their private `ssh-agent -a <sock>` never binds, so `ssh-add` fails with \"Error connecting to agent: No such file or directory\") and both tests in `tests/unit/test_network_guard_local_ipc.py`.\n- Writes to the user's home directory. semgrep opens `~/.semgrep/semgrep.log` and dies with `PermissionError`, so the opengrep/semgrep detector abstains: `tests/unit/test_code_review_conflict_markers.py` and `tests/unit/test_code_review_public_exposure.py` (4 failures, while their negative tests pass falsely after 122 s each) and 2 tests in `tests/unit/grounding/test_conformance.py`.\n- The package index. Isolated builds cannot fetch `hatchling` through the sandbox proxy: the 3 `tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py` errors and `tests/unit/test_attestation_signing.py::test_hook_falls_back_to_git_when_env_unset`.\nThese are not test defects: the suite legitimately exercises an ssh-agent socket, the AF_UNIX allowance of the network guard, a real semgrep, and a real isolated build, and CI hosts provide all of them. The earlier per-test sandbox shims (`tests/_sandbox_capabilities.py`, ticket 985f-0ec5) cannot cover these, because the capability itself is what the test checks.\n\n## Approach\nMake the requirement explicit and enforced instead of producing a misleading red (or, for the semgrep negatives, a false green) after a 25-minute run: `make verify` refuses up front on a host that lacks a capability the suite needs, and says why.\n- New `scripts/check_verify_host.py` (marked `# mechanism-ok: ci_gate scripts/check_verify_host.py — <this ticket>`). It runs 3 operation-based probes, each bounded: (1) bind, listen and connect an AF_UNIX socket in a fresh `tempfile.mkdtemp()` directory; (2) create and delete a uniquely named file directly in `Path.home()`; (3) `python -m pip index versions hatchling --retries 0 --timeout 15 --disable-pip-version-check`, which uses pip's own index and proxy configuration exactly as the isolated builds do. It prints one line per failed probe naming the capability, the error, and the tests that need it, then a closing line saying `make verify` must run where these are available (for Claude Code, outside the sandbox), and exits 1. With all probes passing it prints nothing and exits 0.\n- `Makefile`: a `verify-host` target that runs the script, listed as the FIRST prerequisite of `verify` (`verify: verify-host lint typecheck import-convention test`). `make test` and its two pytest lines stay unchanged, so `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` is unaffected. No skip is added anywhere: on a capable host every test runs as before.\n- Docs: a short \"Where `make verify` can run\" section in `docs/local-dev-env.md` listing the 3 capabilities and the agent-sandbox case, and one sentence in the `make verify` paragraph of `AGENTS.md` pointing to it.\n- No config key, environment variable, or flag is added; the refusal cannot be bypassed from the command line (a host that can run the suite passes the probes).\n\n## Scope\n- `scripts/check_verify_host.py` (new)\n- `tests/unit/test_check_verify_host.py` (new)\n- `Makefile`\n- `docs/local-dev-env.md`\n- `AGENTS.md`\n\n## Testing\n- Unit tests in `tests/unit/test_check_verify_host.py`, each probe driven through an injected seam: all capabilities present gives exit 0 and empty output; an AF_UNIX `PermissionError`, an unwritable home (`HOME` pointed at a read-only temp dir), and a failing pip index probe each give exit 1 with that capability named; 2 failures are both reported in one run.\n- A test asserts `verify-host` is the first prerequisite of `verify` in the Makefile.\n- Manual, recorded on this ticket: inside the agent sandbox `make verify` exits 1 within seconds naming all 3 capabilities; outside it, `verify-host` exits 0 and the run proceeds.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Inside the agent sandbox, `make verify` stops before `lint` with a message naming the denied capabilities (AF_UNIX sockets, home-directory writes, package index), recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] Outside the sandbox the preflight passes silently and `make verify` passes through the shared verify slot.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_check_verify_host.py` covers each probe's pass and fail path and the Makefile ordering.\n- [ ] `docs/local-dev-env.md` and `AGENTS.md` state where `make verify` can run.\n- [ ] Gerrit gives Verified +1.","id":"d492-04db-b79e-428f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"make verify inside the agent sandbox cannot match CI: AF_UNIX sockets, home-directory writes and the package index are denied; refuse up front"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795206129594136001,"uuid":"9342e488-3a43-4072-a361-6bac81b2caf5"}